// A non-writer must be a clean compile error, not a write to whatever file
// descriptor the integer happened to name.
//
// The writer used to be typed int64 (a descriptor) with a SYNTACTIC guard
// restricting the argument to os.Stdout / os.Stderr, because no io.Writer
// existed. It is now a structural writer test, so any type with a
// Write([]byte) (int, error) method is accepted and an int is not.
//
// The check deliberately lives BEFORE the selector-call block in
// type_check_call_expr: that block is gated on !skip_variadic_builtin, and the
// Fprint rows declare zero fixed params, so a check placed inside it silently
// stops running and the failure becomes backend noise instead.
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
	fmt.Fprintln(3, "goes nowhere good")
}
